{%- comment -%}
  ITM Product Group Picker
  ------------------------
  Renders a "product group" collection (a single model available in a run of
  sizes/specs — e.g. Metric Combination Spanners, 20-40 near-identical
  products differing only by size) as ONE hero photo plus a sortable list of
  every size — not N repeated full product cards, which just shows the same
  photo dozens of times and buries the thing a shopper actually needs: "pick
  my size, add to cart, done."

  Desktop: every spec (Size, Jaw Diameter, Ring Diameter, ...) gets its own
  column, and every column header — Model, each spec, Price — is a sort
  button (click once for ascending, again for descending, same convention
  as any spreadsheet/data table).

  Mobile: there's no room for 6+ columns, so it's a native <select> instead
  — the OS's own picker UI is the most reliable "choose one of these" control
  on a phone, next to a small direction toggle. Rows stay the existing
  compact card layout with the always-visible 2-column specs block
  underneath.

  Params:
    - collection (Collection) — required, a collection with
      custom.product_group == true

  Reuses the same .sbc__atc[data-variant-id] class/attribute the parent
  section's existing "Add to cart" click handler already delegates on, so
  no new JS is needed for that part. Sorting itself is plain client-side JS
  reordering the already-rendered <li> elements — the spec VALUES are free
  text ("1-7/16 Inch", "50mm", "102"), not real numbers, so there's no clean
  way to do this as a Liquid/server-side sort; see parseSpecValue below for
  how a value like that becomes a comparable number.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign hero_product = collection.metafields.custom.primary_product_ref.value
  if hero_product == blank
    assign hero_product = collection.products.first
  endif
  assign hero_image = collection.image
  if hero_image == blank and hero_product
    assign hero_image = hero_product.featured_image
  endif

  comment
    Price range across every size in the group, product-page style
    ("From $16.20" or "$16.20 - $24.90" if they're not all the same price).
  endcomment
  assign price_min = null
  assign price_max = null
  for p in collection.products
    if price_min == null or p.price_min < price_min
      assign price_min = p.price_min
    endif
    if price_max == null or p.price_min > price_max
      assign price_max = p.price_min
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Column discovery pass: the union of every spec label across every
    product in the group (first-seen order), not just the first product's —
    a group is broadly consistent, but not perfectly, so building the
    column list off just one product risks silently dropping a column that
    only shows up on a different size. '|||' on both ends of the
    accumulator (not just between entries) so the "contains" check below
    can't false-positive on one label being a plain substring of another
    (e.g. "Ring Diameter" inside "Ring Diameter (mm)").
  endcomment
  assign column_labels_str = '|||'
  for p in collection.products
    capture p_pairs
      render 'itm-spec-parser', product: p
    endcapture
    assign p_pairs = p_pairs | strip
    unless p_pairs == blank
      assign p_tokens = p_pairs | split: ';;'
      for token in p_tokens
        assign tok_label = token | split: '=' | first
        assign needle = '|||' | append: tok_label | append: '|||'
        unless column_labels_str contains needle
          assign column_labels_str = column_labels_str | append: tok_label | append: '|||'
        endunless
      endfor
    endunless
  endfor
  assign column_labels = column_labels_str | split: '|||'
-%}

<div class="itm-pg-picker">
  <div class="itm-pg-picker__hero">
    <div class="itm-pg-picker__hero-media">
      {%- if hero_image -%}
        {{ hero_image | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 40vw, 100vw', widths: '400,600,800,900', alt: collection.title }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'itm-pg-picker__ph-svg' }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Repeats the collection title right beside its own photo, product-page
      style — the page's own H1 (rendered further up by the banner section)
      can be a full scroll away by the time someone's actually looking at
      the size list, especially on mobile.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="itm-pg-picker__hero-info">
      <h2 class="itm-pg-picker__title">{{ collection.title }}</h2>
      <div class="itm-pg-picker__meta">
        <span class="itm-pg-picker__count">{{ collection.products.size }} sizes</span>
        {%- if price_min -%}
          <span class="itm-pg-picker__price-range">
            {%- if price_min == price_max -%}
              {{ price_min | money }}
            {%- else -%}
              From {{ price_min | money }}
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- if collection.description != blank -%}
        <div class="itm-pg-picker__desc rte">{{ collection.description }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Mobile sort control — a native <select>, not a custom dropdown/sheet.
    A single-choice picker is exactly what a <select> is for, and the OS's
    own picker UI (the iOS wheel / Android list) is more reliable and more
    familiar to someone on a phone than a bespoke overlay would be. The
    small ▲/▼ button beside it is the only extra piece needed for direction,
    since a <select> alone has no notion of "click again to reverse".
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="itm-pg-picker__mobile-sort medium-hide large-up-hide">
    <label class="itm-pg-picker__mobile-sort-label" for="PgSortSelect-{{ collection.id }}">Sort by</label>
    <div class="itm-pg-picker__mobile-sort-row">
      <select id="PgSortSelect-{{ collection.id }}" class="itm-pg-picker__mobile-sort-select" data-pg-sort-select>
        <option value="name">Model (A–Z)</option>
        {%- for col in column_labels -%}
          {%- unless col == blank -%}
            <option value="spec:{{ col | escape }}">{{ col }}</option>
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        <option value="price">Price</option>
      </select>
      <button type="button" class="itm-pg-picker__mobile-sort-dir" data-pg-sort-dir aria-label="Reverse sort direction">▲</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="itm-pg-picker__list-wrap">
    <div class="itm-pg-picker__list-head medium-up-hide-not">
      <button type="button" class="itm-pg-picker__sort-btn itm-pg-picker__sort-btn--name" data-pg-sort-key="name">
        Model <span class="itm-pg-picker__sort-arrow"></span>
      </button>
      {%- for col in column_labels -%}
        {%- unless col == blank -%}
          <button type="button" class="itm-pg-picker__sort-btn" data-pg-sort-key="spec:{{ col | escape }}">
            {{ col }} <span class="itm-pg-picker__sort-arrow"></span>
          </button>
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      <button type="button" class="itm-pg-picker__sort-btn itm-pg-picker__sort-btn--price" data-pg-sort-key="price">
        Price <span class="itm-pg-picker__sort-arrow"></span>
      </button>
      <span class="itm-pg-picker__sort-btn itm-pg-picker__sort-btn--actions" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>

    <ul class="itm-pg-picker__list list-unstyled" data-pg-list>
      {%- for product in collection.products -%}
        {%- liquid
          capture row_pairs
            render 'itm-spec-parser', product: product
          endcapture
          assign row_pairs = row_pairs | strip
          assign row_tokens = ''
          unless row_pairs == blank
            assign row_tokens = row_pairs | split: ';;'
          endunless

          comment
            Mobile's always-open specs block still wants plain "Label:
            Value" lines (see the markup below) — rebuild that same flat
            format from the tokens rather than re-parsing the HTML a third
            time.
          endcomment
          assign spec_lines_str = ''
          if row_tokens != ''
            for token in row_tokens
              assign tok_label = token | split: '=' | first
              assign tok_value = token | remove_first: tok_label | remove_first: '='
              assign spec_lines_str = spec_lines_str | append: tok_label | append: ': ' | append: tok_value | append: '|||'
            endfor
          endif
          assign spec_lines = spec_lines_str | split: '|||'
          assign has_specs = false
          if spec_lines.size > 0
            assign has_specs = true
          endif
        -%}
        <li class="itm-pg-picker__item" data-pg-row data-name="{{ product.title | escape }}" data-price="{{ product.price }}">
          <div class="itm-pg-picker__row">
            <a href="{{ product.url }}" class="itm-pg-picker__name">{{ product.title }}</a>

            {%- comment -%} Desktop-only per-column cells — hidden on mobile via CSS. {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- for col in column_labels -%}
              {%- unless col == blank -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign cell_value = ''
                  if row_tokens != ''
                    for token in row_tokens
                      assign tok_label = token | split: '=' | first
                      if tok_label == col
                        assign cell_value = token | remove_first: tok_label | remove_first: '='
                      endif
                    endfor
                  endif
                -%}
                <span class="itm-pg-picker__cell" data-col="{{ col | escape }}" data-value="{{ cell_value | escape }}">{{ cell_value | default: '—' }}</span>
              {%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}

            <span class="itm-pg-picker__price">
              {%- if product.compare_at_price > product.price -%}
                <s class="itm-pg-picker__was">{{ product.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
              {%- endif -%}
              {{ product.price_min | money }}
            </span>
            <div class="itm-pg-picker__actions">
              {%- if product.variants.size == 1 and product.available -%}
                <button class="itm-pg-picker__atc sbc__atc" data-variant-id="{{ product.first_available_variant.id }}">
                  {{- 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t | default: 'Add' -}}
                  <svg class="sbc__atc-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="7" y1="17" x2="17" y2="7"/><polyline points="7 7 17 7 17 17"/></svg>
                </button>
              {%- elsif product.available -%}
                <a href="{{ product.url }}" class="itm-pg-picker__atc itm-pg-picker__atc--options sbc__atc">
                  {{- 'products.product.choose_options' | t | default: 'Options' -}}
                  <svg class="sbc__atc-arrow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="7" y1="17" x2="17" y2="7"/><polyline points="7 7 17 7 17 17"/></svg>
                </a>
              {%- else -%}
                <button class="itm-pg-picker__atc sbc__atc" disabled>{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t | default: 'Sold Out' }}</button>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </div>
          {%- comment -%} Mobile-only — hidden on desktop via CSS, since the row above already has a column per spec there. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if has_specs -%}
            <div class="itm-pg-picker__specs">
              <ul>
                {%- for line in spec_lines -%}
                  <li>{{ line }}</li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
(function () {
  var root = document.currentScript.previousElementSibling;
  {% comment %} Fallback in case the DOM shifted — walk up to find the .itm-pg-picker itself. {% endcomment %}
  var container = document.currentScript.closest ? document.currentScript.parentElement : null;
  var picker = container ? container.querySelector('.itm-pg-picker') : document.querySelector('.itm-pg-picker');
  if (!picker) return;

  var list = picker.querySelector('[data-pg-list]');
  if (!list) return;

  {% comment %}
    Spec values are free text ("1-7/16 Inch", "50mm", "102", "24.6") — this
    pulls out something comparable: mixed fractions ("1-7/16") and plain
    fractions ("7/16") resolve to their decimal value, otherwise it's just
    the first plain number found in the string. Returns null for anything
    with no number at all (a text-only value), which always sorts last
    regardless of direction — a missing/non-numeric spec shouldn't just
    silently land at the top of an ascending sort.
  {% endcomment %}
  function parseSpecValue(str) {
    if (!str) return null;
    str = String(str).trim();
    var mixed = str.match(/^(\d+)\s*-\s*(\d+)\s*\/\s*(\d+)/);
    if (mixed) return parseInt(mixed[1], 10) + (parseInt(mixed[2], 10) / parseInt(mixed[3], 10));
    var frac = str.match(/^(\d+)\s*\/\s*(\d+)/);
    if (frac) return parseInt(frac[1], 10) / parseInt(frac[2], 10);
    var num = str.match(/-?\d+(\.\d+)?/);
    if (num) return parseFloat(num[0]);
    return null;
  }

  function getSortValue(row, key) {
    if (key === 'name') return (row.dataset.name || '').toLowerCase();
    if (key === 'price') return parseFloat(row.dataset.price) || 0;
    if (key.indexOf('spec:') === 0) {
      var col = key.slice(5);
      var cells = row.querySelectorAll('.itm-pg-picker__cell');
      for (var i = 0; i < cells.length; i++) {
        if (cells[i].getAttribute('data-col') === col) {
          return parseSpecValue(cells[i].getAttribute('data-value'));
        }
      }
      return null;
    }
    return null;
  }

  var currentKey = null;
  var currentDir = 1;

  function updateIndicators(key, dir) {
    picker.querySelectorAll('[data-pg-sort-key]').forEach(function (btn) {
      var isActive = btn.getAttribute('data-pg-sort-key') === key;
      btn.classList.toggle('is-active', isActive);
      var arrow = btn.querySelector('.itm-pg-picker__sort-arrow');
      if (arrow) arrow.textContent = isActive ? (dir === 1 ? '▲' : '▼') : '';
    });
    var select = picker.querySelector('[data-pg-sort-select]');
    if (select) select.value = key;
    var dirBtn = picker.querySelector('[data-pg-sort-dir]');
    if (dirBtn) dirBtn.textContent = dir === 1 ? '▲' : '▼';
  }

  function applySort(key, dir) {
    var rows = Array.prototype.slice.call(list.children).filter(function (el) {
      return el.hasAttribute('data-pg-row');
    });
    var isName = key === 'name';
    rows.sort(function (a, b) {
      var av = getSortValue(a, key);
      var bv = getSortValue(b, key);
      if (isName) {
        if (av < bv) return -1 * dir;
        if (av > bv) return 1 * dir;
        return 0;
      }
      var aMissing = (av === null || av === undefined || isNaN(av));
      var bMissing = (bv === null || bv === undefined || isNaN(bv));
      if (aMissing && bMissing) return 0;
      if (aMissing) return 1;
      if (bMissing) return -1;
      return (av - bv) * dir;
    });
    rows.forEach(function (row) { list.appendChild(row); });
    updateIndicators(key, dir);
  }

  picker.querySelectorAll('[data-pg-sort-key]').forEach(function (btn) {
    btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var key = btn.getAttribute('data-pg-sort-key');
      if (currentKey === key) {
        currentDir = currentDir * -1;
      } else {
        currentKey = key;
        currentDir = 1;
      }
      applySort(currentKey, currentDir);
    });
  });

  var mobileSelect = picker.querySelector('[data-pg-sort-select]');
  if (mobileSelect) {
    mobileSelect.addEventListener('change', function () {
      currentKey = mobileSelect.value;
      currentDir = 1;
      applySort(currentKey, currentDir);
    });
  }

  var dirBtn = picker.querySelector('[data-pg-sort-dir]');
  if (dirBtn) {
    dirBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      if (!currentKey) return;
      currentDir = currentDir * -1;
      applySort(currentKey, currentDir);
    });
  }
})();
</script>

<style>
  .itm-pg-picker {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 380px) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 32px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__hero-media {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    background: #f4f4f4;
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__hero-media img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
    mix-blend-mode: multiply;
    display: block;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__ph-svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; opacity: 0.2; }

  .itm-pg-picker__title {
    margin: 16px 0 4px;
    font-size: 22px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__count { color: #666666; }
  .itm-pg-picker__price-range { font-weight: 700; color: #131313; }
  .itm-pg-picker__desc {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #444444;
  }

  /* ── Desktop sort header + rows: flexbox, not a fixed grid, since the
       number of spec columns is data-driven and varies per category. ── */
  .itm-pg-picker__list-head,
  .itm-pg-picker__row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__list-head {
    padding: 0 16px 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e2e2;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__sort-btn {
    flex: 1 1 0;
    min-width: 0;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px;
    border: none;
    background: none;
    padding: 4px 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading-family);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: #888888;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__sort-btn:hover { color: #131313; }
  .itm-pg-picker__sort-btn.is-active { color: #131313; }
  .itm-pg-picker__sort-btn--name { flex: 1.4 1 0; }
  .itm-pg-picker__sort-btn--price { flex: 0.7 1 0; }
  .itm-pg-picker__sort-btn--actions { flex: 0 0 96px; cursor: default; }
  .itm-pg-picker__sort-arrow { font-size: 9px; color: var(--mega-accent, #BD2321); }

  .itm-pg-picker__list { border-top: none; }
  {%- comment -%}
    Zebra striping — exactly two flat shades total (white / grey). The
    specs block (mobile only) has no background of its own — it shows
    whatever colour its parent .itm-pg-picker__item already is, so the
    whole item reads as one solid band.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  .itm-pg-picker__item { border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e2e2; background: #ffffff; }
  .itm-pg-picker__item:nth-child(even) { background: #f4f4f4; }
  .itm-pg-picker__row { padding: 12px 16px; }
  .itm-pg-picker__name {
    flex: 1.4 1 0;
    min-width: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading-family);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #131313;
    text-decoration: none;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__name:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .itm-pg-picker__cell {
    flex: 1 1 0;
    min-width: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #444444;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__price {
    flex: 0.7 1 0;
    min-width: 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #131313;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__was {
    display: block;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 400;
    opacity: 0.55;
    text-decoration: line-through;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__actions {
    flex: 0 0 96px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-end;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__atc {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    height: 34px;
    padding: 0 14px;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: #BD2321;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-family: var(--font-heading-family);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-decoration: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: filter 0.15s ease;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .itm-pg-picker__atc:hover { filter: brightness(0.85); }
  .itm-pg-picker__atc:disabled { opacity: 0.45; cursor: default; pointer-events: none; }

  /* Mobile-only specs block — hidden on desktop, where every spec already
     has its own column in the row above instead. */
  .itm-pg-picker__specs { display: none; }

  /* Mobile sort control — hidden on desktop (medium-hide large-up-hide
     classes already do this, this is belt-and-braces for anyone who
     overrides those utility classes at the section level). */
  .itm-pg-picker__mobile-sort { display: none; }

  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .itm-pg-picker {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
    }
    .itm-pg-picker__title { margin-top: 14px; font-size: 19px; }

    .itm-pg-picker__mobile-sort {
      display: block;
      margin-top: 20px;
      padding: 0 1.5rem;
    }
    .itm-pg-picker__mobile-sort-label {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      color: #666666;
    }
    .itm-pg-picker__mobile-sort-row { display: flex; gap: 8px; }
    .itm-pg-picker__mobile-sort-select {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      min-width: 0;
      height: 44px;
      padding: 0 12px;
      border: 1px solid #d0d0d0;
      border-radius: 4px;
      background: #ffffff;
      font-family: var(--font-body-family);
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #131313;
    }
    .itm-pg-picker__mobile-sort-dir {
      flex: 0 0 44px;
      height: 44px;
      border: 1px solid #d0d0d0;
      border-radius: 4px;
      background: #ffffff;
      font-size: 16px;
      color: #BD2321;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .itm-pg-picker__list-wrap { margin-top: 16px; }
    .itm-pg-picker__list-head { display: none; }
    .itm-pg-picker__cell { display: none; }
    .itm-pg-picker__row {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      padding: 12px;
    }
    .itm-pg-picker__name { flex: 1 1 auto; width: 100%; order: 1; }
    .itm-pg-picker__price { flex: 1 1 auto; order: 2; }
    .itm-pg-picker__actions { flex: 0 0 auto; order: 3; margin-left: auto; }

    .itm-pg-picker__specs { display: block; padding: 4px 12px 12px; }
    {%- comment -%}
      Two columns instead of one long vertical stack — a phone is wide
      enough for "Size / Jaw Diameter / Jaw Height" beside "Ring Diameter /
      Ring Height / Length" rather than wasting the right half of the
      screen on every single spec line.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    .itm-pg-picker__specs ul {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 4px 12px;
    }
    .itm-pg-picker__specs li {
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #444444;
    }
  }
</style>
